  "source": "Toshiba TOSVERT VF-S15 RS485 communication function instruction manual E6581913",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "TOSVERT VF-S15 RS485 Communication Function Instruction Manual (E6581913)",
      "url": "https://www.toshiba.com/tic/datafiles/manuals/S15_RS485_Communication_Manual.pdf"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The register address is the communication number of the manual, read as hexadecimal: FD00 is address 0xFD00. The monitor values of the form FExx are the value held at the last trip; FDxx is the present value.",
    "The inverter answers function 03 for one register or for 2 to 8 consecutive communication numbers. Numbers xxxA to xxxF and xxAx to xxFx do not exist and are skipped in a block read, so read the registers one at a time or in blocks that do not cross those gaps (a missing number returns 0x8000).",
    "Function 06 writes one register and function 16 (0x10) several, to RAM and EEPROM; the command and monitor registers FA00 to FA87 are RAM only. Function 43 (0x2B) returns the maker, the type (for example VFS15-2037PM) and the version.",
    "To control the drive over Modbus set f829 = 1 (Modbus RTU), a unit number in f802, and enable the communication priority bits 14 and 15 of FA00 (or set fmod = 4 and cmod = 2). Changes to f800, f801 and f829 take effect after a reset.",
    "Currents, the output voltage and the DC voltage are reported in 0.01 % of the rated value, not in amperes or volts; use the rated current FE70 (0.1 A) and rated voltage FE71 (0.1 V) to convert.",
    "Negative values are two's complement. Acceleration and deceleration times follow the time unit of f519 (0.1 s or 0.01 s).",
    "The parameter registers listed are the communication ones the manual names; the inverter's own instruction manual has the communication number of every other parameter.",
    "Factory serial settings: 19200 baud, even parity, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit, inverter number 0 (set 1 to 247 for Modbus; 0 is broadcast). The factory protocol is the Toshiba one, not Modbus."
  ],
